```js
try {
    var linkBlock = stampLinkBlock(repoInfo, runUrl, conclusion);
    names.forEach(...);
} finally {
    ...restore token...
}
```

If `stampLinkBlock` throws, the finally restores the token and the exception propagates. `stampLinkBlock` has internal try/catch for the jobs probe but `cli_execute_command` — no wait, the regex part is safe; the probe is in try/catch. So stampLinkBlock effectively doesn't throw. And in the zombie path, `stampValidationChecksForModule` is called unguarded (like in validate-armed where the big try/catch covers it).

The main unguarded call remains `dispatchCiWorkflow(ticket.branch)` at the zombie re-dispatch path.

